# Kiro CLI. Model traffic and account state go to the hosts of the profile's region, us-east-1
# or eu-central-1, the two Kiro offers: runtime serves inference, management the profile and
# subscription state, and the legacy q.<region> host is required beside them. The CLI tab of
# https://kiro.dev/docs/privacy-and-security/firewalls/ is the list, with the purposes.
allow https://runtime.us-east-1.kiro.dev/       tunnel
allow https://management.us-east-1.kiro.dev/    tunnel
allow https://q.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/        tunnel
allow https://runtime.eu-central-1.kiro.dev/    tunnel
allow https://management.eu-central-1.kiro.dev/ tunnel
allow https://q.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/     tunnel

# Sign-in, `kiro-cli login --use-device-flow`: the code is printed, the browser approves it, and
# the tokens are polled for and refreshed at a host by account kind. Google and GitHub accounts
# use Kiro's own, plus the Cognito federation the same page lists for them; Builder ID and IAM
# Identity Center use AWS SSO OIDC in the instance's region — Builder ID's is us-east-1. An
# Identity Center in another region is a project's own
# `allow https://oidc.<region>.amazonaws.com/ tunnel` line: its sign-in fails with
# `error: dispatch failure`, and the proxy log names the refused host.
allow https://prod.us-east-1.auth.desktop.kiro.dev/     tunnel
allow https://cognito-identity.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/ tunnel
allow https://oidc.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/             tunnel

# Absent, of the same list: telemetry.<region>.kiro.dev and
# prod.us-east-1.telemetry.desktop.kiro.dev — telemetry, each attempt a refusal in the log, or
# none with `kiro-cli settings telemetry.enabled false`; prod.download.cli.kiro.dev and
# desktop-release.q.us-east-1.amazonaws.com — updates and installer downloads, off in the image
# (app.disableAutoupdates); cli.kiro.dev — the install script.
